### ❓ Suggested Questions

1.  A car starts from rest and reaches a speed of $20 m/s$ in $4$ seconds. Calculate its uniform acceleration.
2.  Can an object have zero velocity but non-zero uniform acceleration? (Hint: Think about a ball thrown upwards at its peak).
3.  How does the Distance-Time graph of uniform acceleration differ from that of constant velocity?